RF.put("questb:b63",{"8703":{"id":8703,"t":"Ring of Eternal Justice","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Magisterial Ring, 2 Vermillion Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Magisterial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Vermillion Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Eternal Justice\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8623":{"id":8623,"t":"Stormcaller's Diadem","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'lor's Diadem Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormcaller's Diadem\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Horde Class Shaman Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8623\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stormcaller's Diadem this quest\nBring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8543":{"id":8543,"t":"The Horde Needs More Tin Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 tin bars to Grunt Maug in Durotar.\n20 Tin Bar","desc":"Very good, I see that you are serious about the war. I'm a little edgy waiting for it to start though, which means I'm going to get angry if you don't start bringing in the goods faster. Maybe I can just practice on you instead.\nHar! Maybe not, 'cuz then who would bring me back the tin bars?","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Very good, I see that you are serious about the war. I'm a little edgy waiting for it to start though, as I'm sure you are as well, ‹class›. It will be glorious when it begins. The Horde running over the sands of the Silithus desert, weapons in hand, charging headlong into the insect masses. Great honor will be had that day by all!\nHar! But first we need more tin bars. Funny how such a small thing may make such a huge difference, don't you think?","done":"Throm'ka, ‹name›. You honor me and the Horde with your tin bars. I will put them on the stack and then they will come and make things from them. And then when that is all done we will go to war and show the puny Alliance how to fight the bugs.\nNow bring me back more tin bars!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.1,"y":65,"n":"Grunt Maug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8383":{"id":8383,"t":"Remember Alterac Valley!","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor","desc":"The Battle in Alterac Valley rages on, ‹name›! Have you done your part as of late, ‹name›?","done":"You continue to honor the Alliance, ‹name›. The Horde will be crushed before long if we keep our efforts up.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"6943":{"id":6943,"t":"Call of Air - Ichman's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Commander's Medal Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Frostwolf in Alterac Valley , Irondeep Trogg in Alterac Valley and 4 more","back":"Their spirits are low, soldier. After our last failed air strike against the Horde, they refuse to fly! It is up to you to bolster their morale.\nReturn to the battlefield and strike at the heart of the Frostwolf's command. Take down their commanders and guardians. Return to me with as many of their medals as you can stuff in your pack! I promise you, when my gryphons see the bounty and smell the blood of our enemies, they will fly again! Go now!","done":"Can you see it? Look at them, soldier! They're coming around... Soon, Ichman's flight will once again strike at the heart of the valley! Stormpike will rule the skies!\nStart Wing Commander Ichman Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Ichman Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6943","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6383":{"id":6383,"t":"The Ashenvale Hunt","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"There are three legendary creatures that make up the Ashenvale Hunt; you may seek them and test yourself against their cunning and might. In the process, you will hopefully learn something about yourself. The creatures are: the bear Ursangous, the nightsaber cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon.\nThe creatures of the Ashenvale Hunt are powerful, and you may find that you'll need aid in bringing them down. If you should best them, bring me proof of your deed.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1023":{"id":1023,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":21,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Glowing Gem and return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar with Teronis' Journal.\nGlowing Gem Saltspittle Oracle 10 % , Saltspittle Muckdweller 10 % , Saltspittle Warrior 10 % , Saltspittle Puddlejumper 10 %\nProvided: Teronis' Journal","desc":"As you rummage through Teronis' belongings, you find a journal that is still in good condition.\nYou take the journal and leave Teronis' corpse as is.\nThe only thing left to do is find the gem Teronis was seeking. Raene mentioned it being in the area. Perhaps the murlocs have it...","rew":"Experience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ah, welcome back, ‹name›.","done":"This is terrible, ‹name›. Teronis is dead?!\nThe time for mourning will come, but for now we must focus our efforts. I shall send some of the Sentinels to recover Teronis' body as soon as possible.\nYou have Teronis' journal and the gem he was seeking. Do you think you're capable of completing his task? I would rest much better knowing his death was not in vain.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":20.3,"y":42.3,"n":"Teronis' Corpse","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3503":{"id":3503,"t":"Meeting with the Master","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"There was a time when I could ask whatever I wished from those who sought out my master. But now, you need only ask and I will send you to him.\nIt is upsetting to me, but I do not question his orders. I can only take enjoyment in making fun of the ridiculous clothes you wear or the pathetic look on your face. Even that bores me...\nEven this rambling bores me! Do you wish to see my master or not?","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":28.1,"y":50.1,"n":"Sanath Lim-yo","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"703":{"id":703,"t":"Barbecued Buzzard Wings","lv":40,"min":33,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Buzzard Wings to Rigglefuzz.\n4 Buzzard Wing Searing Roc 43.6 % , Fire Roc 43.1 % , Roc 42.3 % , Sky Shadow 42 % and 4 more","desc":"Oh yes, my barbecued buzzard wings are a favorite! The sauce is rich and the meat is tangy. And the smell will bring the hungry running from miles away!\nI have everything I need to cook up a batch. Everything...except the buzzard wings!\nIf you want some then get me the buzzard wings. Bring me enough, and I might even share the recipe with you!","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Barbecued Buzzard Wing Recipe: Barbecued Buzzard Wing\nExperience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Did you bring me my wings?","done":"Ah, I'll get started on those wings right away. I can almost taste them already!\nAnd here's the recipe in case you want to make them yourself!\nBadlands Riverglades","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.4,"y":52.9,"n":"Rigglefuzz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4063":{"id":4063,"t":"The Rise of the Machines","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and slay Golem Lord Argelmach. Return his head to Lotwil. You will also need to collect 10 Intact Elemental Cores from the Ragereaver Golems and Warbringer Constructs protecting Argelmach. You know this because you are psychic.\nHead of Argelmach Golem Lord Argelmach\n10 Intact Elemental Core Molten War Golem 80 % , Wrath Hammer Construct 80 % , Ragereaver Golem 80 % , Warbringer Construct 80 %","desc":"This can't be Argelmach! Argelmach was killed ten years ago. How can I be sure? I was the one who killed him.\nHe was a despicable dwarf, hell-bent on twisting my life's work to meet his diabolical needs. It seems that the wicked always find a way to escape justice.\nIf this is Argelmach's handiwork then he must be destroyed. I will need samplings of his latest creations. With the proper samples, I may be able to stop this uprising. The creations guard Argelmach in Blackrock Depths.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAzure Moon Amice Raincaster Drape Basaltscale Armor Lavaplate Gauntlets\nMoney: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"Was it him? Was he really alive?","done":"What is this?!? This head is not flesh. This is some sort of dark iron creation: A shadow of Argelmach - ANOTHER machine! I suspect that your destruction of Argelmach will be short lived as another shall rise to take 'its' place soon.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"5103":{"id":5103,"t":"Hot Fiery Death","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Someone in this world must know what to do with these gauntlets. Good luck!","desc":"The only thing that remains of this human are some charred bones. He seems to have died within arms reach of what he was after - unfired plate gauntlets.\nPerhaps you should grab the gauntlets and get out of the fire?","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"What the...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2783":{"id":2783,"t":"Petty Squabbles","lv":57,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the Fallen Hero of the Horde at the border of the Blasted Lands and the swamp.","desc":"We fight the wrong enemy, ‹name›.\nThe true power in these lands continues to grow in strength and number while we squabble over scorched earth with orcs.\nDo we continue to fight a war in these lands against the Horde, only to be routed one day by the armies of the Burning Legion? It is futile.\nPut your differences aside, ‹name›, speak with the fallen hero of the Horde. He knows the truth behind the Blasted Lands.","rew":"Experience: 4,500","done":"The Alliance wishes to assist?\nI thought to never see this day again. A day in which the Alliance fights side by side with the Horde against a common enemy.\nIt shall be... we will unite.\nBlasted Lands Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":67.6,"y":19.3,"n":"Ambassador Ardalan","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"3823":{"id":3823,"t":"Extinguish the Firegut","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 15 Firegut Ogre-Mages, 7 Firegut Ogres, and 7 Firegut Ogre Brutes, and return to Oralius when you are finished.\nFiregut Ogre Mage slain : 0/ 15\nFiregut Ogre slain : 0/ 7\nFiregut Brute slain : 0/ 7","desc":"We must strike at our enemies before they strike at us!\nI'll make this brief, soldier.\nThe Firegut ogres of the Burning Steppes are allies of the Blackrock orcs. They work closely with those vile orcs, keeping the mineral rich Dreadmaul Rock guarded and the supply lines open at all times.\nLeave your mark, ‹name›. Cripple their forces and return to me when the job is done.\n<Oralius grabs at the air and makes a choking motion.>\nI WILL KILL YOU, WINKY!","rew":"Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"There is not nearly enough blood on your uniform, soldier!","done":"Outstanding, soldier! The orcs and ogres will be reeling from this blow for minutes, maybe even hours!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Oralius","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"4223":{"id":4223,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes.","desc":"<Magistrate Solomon sighs.>\nYou must return to the Burning Steppes, ‹name›. As a deputy of Stormwind, you will be required to report to Marshal Maxwell. Good luck.","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"<Marshal Maxwell laughs.>\nRedridge Mountains Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"4463":{"id":4463,"t":"Libram of Rumination","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Black Diamond Borer Beetle 5.2 % , Dark Keeper Uggel 4.6 % , Crest Killer 3.8 % , Burrowing Thundersnout 3.6 % and 4 more\nBlack Blood of the Tormented\nGizzard Gum\nLibram of Rumination Veteran Irondeep Raider 2.9 % , Seasoned Coldmine Explorer 1.3 % in Alterac Valley , The Behemoth 1 % , Champion Coldmine Surveyor 0.7 % in Alterac Valley and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Arcanum of Rumination","back":"Present the components, mortal.\nI will also require payment in the form of thirty gold pieces for this creation.","done":"Take your trinket, fool. Leave me to my studies!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.6,"n":"Mathredis Firestar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97903":{"id":97903,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Rawrk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill with your profession.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":54,"y":42,"n":"Rawrk","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94223":{"id":94223,"t":"Craftsmans writ silver skeleton key","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Silver Skeleton Key\nSilver Skeleton Key","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Silver Skeleton Key, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"<After following the instructions on the writ, you find yourself deep in a crypt surrounded by undead. There is a note on a nearby trunk.>\nWhoever first reads this will be the first to learn of my death. I am a mere caretaker of the Raven Hill Cemetery, whose presence is largely forgotten by even his employers at Darkshire. I have no heir upon whom to bestow my vast wealth. I have since stashed it away, in this box, for who or whatever manages to open it.","done":"<With the undead hordes endlessly gathering nearby and no sign of others, you choose to make use of your Silver Skeleton Key to effortlessly open the chest.\nDespite the claims of impressive riches, the trunk is nearly empty. At the very least there is enough present to cover some of the cost of this ordeal.>","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":26.2,"y":36.3,"n":"Battered Trunk","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94303":{"id":94303,"t":"Craftsmans writ thick leather ammo pouch","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Thick Leather Ammo Pouch\nThick Leather Ammo Pouch","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Thick Leather Ammo Pouch, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Thick Leather Ammo Pouch Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94303","cats":["crafting"]},"7903":{"id":7903,"t":"Evil Bat Eyes","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Evil Bat Eye Bloodseeker Bat 40.9 % in Zul'Gurub , Duskwing 28.8 % , Monstrous Plaguebat 28.4 % , Plaguebat 27.6 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Do you ever find yourself wandering in a cave, late at night, looking for adventure? You do? Really? Well, then you've seen the creepy eyes of bats staring at you from high up, waiting for you to let down your guard so they can suck your blood!\nScary thought, don't you think? Of course! It's no doubt that bat eyes are scary!\nWill you bring me some evil bat eyes, ‹name›? I want them for... something I'm designing. Something scary.\nYou can get them from the bats of the Eastern Plaguelands.","done":"Great! You got the eyes! I hope hunting those bats was frightening for you, because if it scared a brave ‹class› like yourself, then those eyes will certainly scare our Faire visitors.\nTake these tickets, ‹name›, and thank you for your service.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"8223":{"id":8223,"t":"More Glowing Scorpid Blood","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Glowing Scorpid Blood Firetail Scorpid 30.3 % , Stonelash Pincer 29.4 % , Stonelash Flayer 28.2 % , Deathlash Scorpid 21.2 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","back":"That scorpid blood is working out great, ‹name›! It's amazing how a little sparkle and shine can create a prized bauble out of an otherwise piece of junk. The patrons love the stuff, and love is what it's all about, don't you think...\nYou've been a big help to me, ‹name›, and although I don't have a great need for more glowing scorpid blood, if you bring me more then I'll still trade you some tickets.","done":"Thanks again, ‹name›. Here are your tickets!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"943":{"id":943,"t":"The Absent Minded Prospector","lv":24,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Archaeologist's Gown.","obj":"Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor wants you to bring him the Stone of Relu and Flagongut's Fossil.\nStone of Relu Mottled Raptor 7.5 % , Mottled Screecher 7.5 % , Mottled Scytheclaw 7.5 % , Mottled Razormaw 7.5 %\nFlagongut's Fossil Flagongut's Fossil","desc":"Prospector Whelgar now holds the original fossil at his site in the Wetlands. When I discovered the Stone of Relu, I believed it to be the key to unlocking the mystery of the fossil.\nWhile I traveled on the road to meet Whelgar, I was attacked by raptors and the relic was lost. I don't know which one of the mottled beasts swallowed the relic but if you can retrieve it, I can unleash the power of these artifacts.\nBring me both the Stone of Relu, and the original fossil he holds.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRelic Blade Skullchipper Archaeologist's Gown\nNew in Forever: Archaeologist's Gown.\nExperience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"With the Stone of Relu I will be able to release the hidden secrets of my fossil as well as Remtravel's fossil from Darkshore, ‹name›.","done":"Most excellent, ‹name›!\nNow to see if I can use the stone to decipher the powers of the fossils.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.8,"y":60.4,"n":"Archaeologist Flagongut","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6143":{"id":6143,"t":"Other Fish to Fry","lv":36,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Other Fish to Fry .","obj":"Slay 7 Slitherblade Myrmidon, 7 Slitherblade Naga, and 5 Slitherblade Sorceresses, and then talk to Drulzegar at Shadowprey in Desolace.\nSlitherblade Myrmidon slain : 0/ 7\nSlitherblade Naga slain : 0/ 7\nSlitherblade Sorceress slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Maybe you heard or maybe you haven't... my crew and I was out fishing near Ranazjar Isle, north of the wrecked ship off the coast up north. We used to fish there all the time; now all I do is think of a way to seek revenge for my fallen comrades.\nThe naga attacked us one morning, killing everyone except me.\nMe conscience can't handle the guilt, ‹class›; I need you to go and fry them naga for me. I'll make the effort worth your while; you think you can help me with that?","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I still hear their voices crying for help when the naga unleashed their chaos over us. If I didn't have this bad knee, I'd go and help you kill those blasted naga!\nYou can usually guarantee to find them deep in the coral reefs below the surface... lurking... scheming...","done":"As sweet as it is hearing the news that the naga have been vanquished, my heart still feels empty. For the rest of my life I will be dedicated to having them all killed.\nHere mon, your reward as I promised. It's small in comparison to the gratification of knowing the naga fried for their hated act upon my crew.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":23.3,"y":72.9,"n":"Drulzegar Skraghook","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7503":{"id":7503,"t":"The Greatest Race of Hunters","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nThe Greatest Race of Hunters A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: The Greatest Race of Hunters","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: The Greatest Race of Hunters End Lorekeeper Mykos Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7503","cats":["dire-maul"]},"223":{"id":223,"t":"Worgen in the Woods","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Calor's note to Jonathan Carevin.\nCalor's Note\nProvided: Calor's Note","desc":"Here you go, ‹name›. Bring this message to Master Carevin.\n<He quickly removes a piece of faded parchment and offers it to you.>\nA few more like you, and we will outnumber the Night Watch! Perhaps then we could complete the work that we few carry on today.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCloak of the Faith Shield of the Faith\nYou will also receive:\nConsecrated Wand\nExperience: 3,150\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, what is it? Make it quick, I've pressing matters to attend to.","done":"Excuse me for my cold reception, ‹name›, but as I'm sure you can tell, I am an extremely busy man. I see that you have impressed Calor--and I assure you, that is no small feat--and that he has given his recommendation.\nThere are unsavory types afoot, ‹name›, and we can use the help of all who have proven themselves. We battle against demons, the undead, and those who would provide them aid. Be vigilant, be wary, and trust none who would not give aid to our cause.\nGlory under the Light.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Calor","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":49,"n":"Jonathan Carevin","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"5503":{"id":5503,"t":"Argent Dawn Commission","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Commission\nExperience: 550\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer.\nWhile under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. Procure these insignia and bring them to me. For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token.\nAchieve your destiny, ‹class› join the fight today!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9183":{"id":9183,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Radiant Circlet","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 3 Radiant Circlets and the Craftsman's Writ - Radiant Circlet - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Radiant Circlet\n3 Radiant Circlet\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Radiant Circlet","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order BS-80:\n3 Radiant Circlets.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"I still can't believe Metz expects our troops to wear this low-quality garbage to protect against the freezing attacks of the Scourge.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"783":{"id":783,"t":"A Threat Within","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Marshal McBride.","desc":"I hope you strapped your belt on tight, young ‹class›, because there is work to do here in Northshire.\nAnd I don't mean farming.\nThe Stormwind guards are hard pressed to keep the peace here, with so many of us in distant lands and so many threats pressing close. And so we're enlisting the aid of anyone willing to defend their home. And their alliance.\nIf you're here to answer the call, then speak with my superior, Marshal McBride. He's inside the abbey behind me.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Ah, good. Another volunteer. We're getting a lot of you these days.\nI hope it's enough.\nThe human lands are threatened from without, and so many of our forces have been marshaled abroad. This, in turn, leaves room for corrupt and lawless groups to thrive within our borders.\nIt is a many-fronted battle we wage, ‹name›. Gird yourself for a long campaign.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.2,"y":42.9,"n":"Deputy Willem","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91743":{"id":91743,"t":"Rascally rodents","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve 8 Stolen Books from kobolds in Northshire Valley and return them to Brother Paxton.\n8 Stolen Book","desc":"Those awful kobolds are eating my books! You have to get them back before they devour my whole library.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you rescued my books yet, Braiknok?!","done":"Thank you so much! Here! Take one of these how-to books. I don't need them.\nBut there's still so many books missing. The kobolds don't seem to be eating them. So, why do they want them?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3903":{"id":3903,"t":"Milly Osworth","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Milly Osworth.","desc":"You've shown yourself a dependable ‹class›, ‹name›. Dependable, and not afraid to get your hands dirty, eh?\nI have a friend, Milly Osworth, who's in some trouble. She's over with her wagon on the other side of the abbey, near the stable. I'm sure she could use a pair of hands like yours.","rew":"Experience: 35\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Oh, Deputy Willem told you to speak with me? He's a brave man and always willing to help, but his duties keep him stuck at Northshire Abbey and I'm afraid the problem I have today is beyond him.\nPerhaps you can help me?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.2,"y":42.9,"n":"Deputy Willem","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":50.7,"y":39.3,"n":"Milly Osworth","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"95663":{"id":95663,"t":"Dragonmaw rumors","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to the Wetlands and meet the Deathstalker Agent in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp.","desc":"The Dragonmaw are a formidable clan.\nThey're known for binding magic strong enough to make dragons serve, and rumor claims they're preparing some display of it in the Wetlands. Whether truth or bluster, the Deathstalkers can't act on half-formed whispers. Titanic winds carried only that much to me.\nA deathstalker agent needs a hand in the hills above the Dragonmaw encampment. Meet her there. She'll reveal the next steps.\nArathi Highlands Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Zaruk","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.4,"y":59.2,"n":"Deathstalker Agent","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"2863":{"id":2863,"t":"Alpha Strike","lv":43,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 5 Woodpaw Alphas and return to Hadoken Swiftstrider within one hour.\nWoodpaw Alpha slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The plan is for various leaders of the gnolls - Alphas as they call themselves - to be taken down within rapid succession. If we're able to execute this sort of swift and precise devastation against them, it would cause chaos in their ranks. Perhaps it would also drive a message through their thick flea-bitten heads that we can and will destroy them!\nI want you to be the messenger of my will; eliminate five of their Alphas within one hour for this to work ‹name›, or we'll remain at this impasse!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Time is running out, ‹name›! If you're not here to report that you've taken out the Alphas, then you're wasting time!","done":"You've done as I have asked, and for that I salute you. Take this small reward as compensation for your efforts, ‹name›.\nWith their numbers thinned and their leaders slain, the gnolls will think twice about storming the camp. This doesn't conclude the issue at hand, however...\nThere must be some reason why the gnolls have been whipped into such a frenzied state. Before they have a chance to regroup though, I want to find out what is causing it.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2943":{"id":2943,"t":"Return to Troyas","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the book to Troyas Moonbreeze in Feathermoon Stronghold.\nFeralas: A History\nProvided: Feralas: A History","desc":"Here it is, ‹name›. Please, take care of my book.\nNow, hurry along. I'm sure Troyas is eager for your return.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Have you been to Darnassus?","done":"You have brought a book along. Excellent!\nTeldrassil Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Troyas Moonbreeze","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6623":{"id":6623,"t":"Horde Trauma","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Doctor Gregory Victor about joining the ranks of Horde Trauma.","desc":"Doctor ‹name›, I presume. It is a pleasure to see you again.\nI have some wonderful news for you! Doctor Gregory Victor, chief physician of Horde Trauma has made a personal request for you to join him at Hammerfall. This could be the opportunity of a lifetime! I would give anything to be given a chance to study under the great Doctor Gregory Victor! Do not squander this opportunity!","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"Wonderful. Put on your scrubs, we are to start at once!\nOrgrimmar Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.2,"y":84.6,"n":"Arnok","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":36.9,"n":"Doctor Gregory Victor","e":1}],"cats":["first-aid"]},"6063":{"id":6063,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Webwood Lurker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"As a hunter, it is important to remember the responsibility you hold in your hands. Nature is not a power that can be bent to obey our desires; it is one that is to be respected and acknowledged as something stronger than your very existence.\n‹name›, you must prove your understanding of this before you will gain the ability to tame an animal to be your companion.\nYour first task is to take this taming rod. With it, you will be able to tame a webwood lurker. Tame it, and practice your skills as a hunter.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"You will learn, ‹name›, and one day you will be a great ‹class›.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›! You are quite a fast learner.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"94863":{"id":94863,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.\nTame a Gray Forest Wolf\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You've alraedy mastered taming a boar, now it's time for the next lesson. The forest holds fiercer companions, and with care, you can earn their trust.\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Gray Forest Wolf. Remember, nature's balance must be respected. Prove your skill as a hunter once more.","back":"With learning, Darlin, comes mastery.","done":"Well done, Darlin! You're quite in tune with the beast.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Josephine Carson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9263":{"id":9263,"t":"Investigate the Scourge of Orgrimmar","lv":10,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 625 experience instead of 650, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Collect three Dim Necrotic Stones from the Scourge outside Orgrimmar and investigate the glowing runic circles near their encampment.\n3 Dim Necrotic Stone Skeletal Soldier 35 % , Spectral Apparition 35 % , Spectral Spirit 31 % , Skeletal Trooper 31 %","desc":"The Lich King has sent his undead upon our very doorstep; we cannot remain idle! Surely you will step up to defend Orgrimmar from these accursed invaders?\nThere are strange runic circles outside, glowing with the same energy that surrounds the undead and the Necropolis above. They have significance, I'm certain, and I want you to find out what. Thin the numbers of those aberrations while you're at it; bring me proof of their death along with your results, and I will reward you. Go!","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625","back":"Have you investigated the invasion yet? There's no time for dawdling!","done":"Hmm. From what you've told me, the voices within the circles... they must be used for communication of some kind. I shudder to think what unnatural minds are contacted through such magic. Regardless, you seem to have emerged whole and sane. The Argent Dawn appreciates your service.\nOrgrimmar Elwynn Forest Tirisfal Glades Dun Morogh Mulgore Durotar Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Lieutenant Dagel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"9343":{"id":9343,"t":"Tabard of the Argent Dawn","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"10 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nTabard of the Argent Dawn","back":"You have aided our cause greatly, ‹name›. If you wish, I can make available the tabard of the Argent Dawn. We are proud to have you among our allies.","done":"Take this tabard and wear it proudly. Perhaps your deeds might inspire others to take up arms in support of our fight against the Scourge.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"97263":{"id":97263,"t":"Your package has arrived","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Eldrun's misplaced package.\nProvided: Misplaced Package","desc":"<Several misplaced packages have been left by the mailbox. You note that one of them is marked for delivery from Aerie Peak, to Ironforge, to Eldrun Stormbreaker. It is marked \"urgent.\">","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 0 silver, 8 copper Experience: 45","back":"What's that you've got there?","done":"What! I've been going to the mailbox by the bank every day looking for this package! This city needs to figure out its layout. Not easy to navigate like Aerie Peak!\nLet's see what I've got... totem carving tools... spare axe... some kind of goblin device? I didn't order that! Ah, I'll just send it back.\nEr, uh... I mean... thank you for bringing all of this to me. Here's a little something for your trouble.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":72.3,"y":48.4,"n":"Misplaced Packages","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":47.4,"y":13.6,"n":"Eldrun Stormbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8863":{"id":8863,"t":"Festival Dumplings","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 50.","obj":"Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\n8 Festival Dumplings","back":"If you are hungry, then you have come to the right place my friend! Dumplings are the traditional food of the Lunar Festival; it has been served since the time of the first Lunar Festival, and I am pleased to be able to offer it at this one. In exchange for just a single coin of ancestry, I will share with you a sampling of one of the tastiest dishes you will ever enjoy!","done":"Excellent - please enjoy these dumplings with my compliments. While they are but a small token of appreciation for the honor you have brought upon yourself through your actions, I think you will enjoy them all the same.\nShould you have any more coins of ancestry, I stand ready to offer you a wide array of items in exchange.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9103":{"id":9103,"t":"Plagueheart Robe","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Plagueheart Robe if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Robe, 25 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Robe\n25 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Robe\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Robe.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8943":{"id":8943,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Dreadmist Belt and a set of Dreadmist Wraps to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nDreadmist Belt Scholomance Necromancer 1.7 % in Scholomance , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 1.3 % in Stratholme , Thuzadin Necromancer 1.2 % in Stratholme , Crimson Conjuror 0.9 % in Stratholme and 1 more\nDreadmist Wraps Lorekeeper Polkelt 17 % in Scholomance , Scholomance Necromancer 0 % in Scholomance","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Belt Deathmist Wraps\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"3103":{"id":3103,"t":"Hallowed Letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Letter and speak to Priestess Anetta in Northshire Abbey.\nHallowed Letter\nProvided: Hallowed Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Priestess Anetta, our local priest trainer. I wouldn't hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, at last you've come. I knew you would find your way to me. The Holy Light shines upon you, and the path you've chosen. These times are harsh--the Burning Legion still has a presence upon Azeroth, the entirety of Kalimdor seeks new ways to defend itself from its own tribulations, and it is up to you to aid as many as you can.","done":"As you grow in experience, return to me and I will do what I can to impart my knowledge upon you. Until then, go with compassion in your heart, and let wisdom be your guide. Remember, the world only becomes a better place if you make it so.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Priestess Anetta","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5663":{"id":5663,"t":"Touch of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"Aelthalyste sent word out to all her priests. We're to direct the younger of our order to the Undercity for more training. If you truly count yourself among our faithful, then you should return there also.\nYou can find Aelthalyste in the War Quarter deep in the Undercity.","rew":"You will learn: Touch of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"Ah, good, another has arrived. Time may not matter to me, but to you it is of the essence. There is much for you to learn and there is much I wish to teach you. You simply must prove your worth. Do that, and you shall be greatly rewarded.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":52.2,"n":"Dark Cleric Beryl","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"143":{"id":143,"t":"Messenger to Westfall","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Magistrate Solomon wants you to take his written plea to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\nSolomon's Plea to Westfall\nProvided: Solomon's Plea to Westfall","desc":"Something odd is afoot with the Stormwind Army. They should have been here in force by now. Time is a luxury we don't have, however. I will not stand by and watch the people of Lakeshire give their lives without trying to enlist more help. I've heard word of a people's militia forming in Westfall.\nTake this plea to their leader, Gryan Stoutmantle. Perhaps Stoutmantle's men can lend some support here until the King sends reserves.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hail, ‹class›. What business do you have with The People's Militia?","done":"Good Messenger, you have served your master well.\nRedridge Mountains Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"96783":{"id":96783,"t":"A way in","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Steal a Syndicate uniform from Northfold Manor to infiltrate Stromgarde Keep.","desc":"Stromgarde Keep is one of the Syndicate's largest strongholds. Many of the organization's most important dealings take place behind its walls.\nI have received word of a certain trade taking place between members of the Syndicate somewhere in Arathi Highlands, and I'm certain the details of this trade can be found somewhere in Stromgarde.\nTo infiltrate the keep without arousing suspicion, you'll need a disguise. See if you can find one among the Syndicate outside the keep, at Northfold Manor.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":85,"y":80.4,"n":"Myrokos Silentform","s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"5343":{"id":5343,"t":"Barov Family Fortune","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Weldon Barov when you have completed this task.\nThe Deed to Brill The Deed to Brill in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Caer Darrow The Deed to Caer Darrow in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Southshore The Deed to Southshore in Scholomance\nThe Deed to Tarren Mill The Deed to Tarren Mill in Scholomance","desc":"My dear brother Alexi. What a fool I was to spare his life. I looked into the face of the enemy, one of the undead, and let him live.\n<Weldon spits.>\nHe now searches for MY inheritance. This simply cannot happen.\nFind my family's deeds before that vile retch gets his boney hands upon them and I shall reward you with vast riches. They lay in the ruins of the Scholomance. Make haste!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"Bow your head in my presence, ‹race›. I am a noble, after all, and you are a copperless peasant.","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Now to secure my inheritance...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.5,"y":83.7,"n":"Weldon Barov","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"7023":{"id":7023,"t":"Greatfather Winter is Here!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Ironforge.","desc":"Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend! Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter, who's currently in Ironforge! If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil. Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!\nAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year. We have a great selection to choose from. Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.\nIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.\nUndercity Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":68.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Nardstrum Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"63":{"id":63,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat the Corrupt Manifestation of Water and place the Corrupted Manifestation's Bracers along with the Remaining Drops of Purest Water on the Brazier of Everfount in Silverpine Forest.\nCorrupt Manifestation's Bracers Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water\nRemaining Drops of Purest Water\nProvided: Remaining Drops of Purest Water","desc":"Along the coast of Silverpine, west of the Sepulcher, you will find a shrine that has become tainted by the plague. The spirits there no longer speak to our people and it will be up to you to defeat the manifestation and cleanse the pool.\nTake the elemental's bracers, along with the remaining drops of Brine's potion, and place them on the brazier. The ritual should be enough to summon a pure spirit for you to communicate with.\nBring me proof the task is done, and I will reward you with your totem.","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"The brazier still reflects the ambient light from the area, and the flame shifts slightly as you move closer.\nThe corruption along the hills seems to have kept its distance, and besides the missing components, the brazier looks prepared for the ritual to summon a cleansed manifestation of water.","done":"You place the bracers atop the brazier and then pour the remaining drops of Brine's potion into the flame. The drops crackle as they hit the flame and you begin to incant the simple words Islen taught you....\nThe Barrens Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":38.3,"y":44.6,"n":"Brazier of Everfount","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1103":{"id":1103,"t":"Call of Water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Water Sapta to Tiev Mordune in Silverpine Forest if you failed to speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water.\nWater Sapta","desc":"Greetin's, brotha/sista! Have you too come to purify the waters here and prove your understandin' to Islen?\nI've just defeated the corrupt water spirit meself, and I'm just 'bout to put da bracers and remaining drops o' water on the brazier.\nWhat's dat? Ahhh. Tiev understan' all too well when somethin' goes wrong. Well, Tiev can help you plenty if you be needin' to see the pure water spirit again.\nBring me a water sapta from Islen as proof that you be ready, an' I'll wait to turn in me parts.","back":"Ya have the sapta, brotha?\nI know another that had trouble after defeating da corrupt water spirit--seems he waited too long and he came out of the spirit world too quick fer his taste. Hate to see dat happen to another, so I'll just wait here fer a bit to make sure no one else be needin' me help.","done":"Ahhh, den yur ready...\nI'll put me items in the brazier den, and you c'n talk wit' da spirit too.\nAn' dontchu worry none 'bout seein' into da spirit world wit' da sapta... ol' Tiev know a trick or two 'bout how da sapta magic works.\nCome now, head down wit' me to the shrine and let's speak to da spirits together, brotha.\nSilverpine Forest The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":37.3,"y":44.2,"n":"Tiev Mordune","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8303":{"id":8303,"t":"Anachronos","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris.\nProvided: The War of the Shifting Sands","desc":"It is time, ‹name›.\nI must apologize for keeping so much in secret. Enemies abound, even under our very noses. Please, read from this tome and learn. Take the knowledge I give to you and seek out our master.","done":"You are the hope of Kalimdor, ‹name›.\nSilithus Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":36.4,"n":"Baristolth of the Shifting Sands","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8783":{"id":8783,"t":"Extraordinary Materials","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Enchanted Thorium Bars and 2 Enchanted Leather to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IX in order to complete this quest.\n2 Enchanted Thorium Bar\n2 Enchanted Leather sold by Lhara\nLogistics Task Briefing IX\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing IX","desc":"Vargus, Cenarion Hold's blacksmith, has requested enchanted materials to be used in the crafting of powerful weapons for our forces. Obtain these and bring them directly to Vargus so that Cenarion Hold's troops may continue to be well equipped.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"9023":{"id":9023,"t":"The Perfect Poison","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dirk Thunderwood at Cenarion Hold wants you to bring him Venoxis's Venom Sac and Kurinnaxx's Venom Sac.\nVenoxis's Venom Sac High Priest Venoxis in Zul'Gurub\nKurinnaxx's Venom Sac Kurinnaxx in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj","desc":"My brother and I run the poison operations out of the manor Ravenholdt.\nLord Ravenholdt tasked me to track down a new and extremely effective poison compound that can be crafted from the venom sacs of the inhabitants of Zul'Gurub and the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj.\nThere are two particularly venomous beasts residing in those blasted ruins that possess what it is that we might be looking for, ‹class›. Bring me a venom sac from the beasts Kurinnaxx and Venoxis and we would be eternally grateful.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRavenholdt Slicer Shivsprocket's Shiv The Thunderwood Poker Doomulus Prime Fahrad's Reloading Repeater Simone's Cultivating Hammer\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"This ain't no smash and grab job, ‹name›. You're gonna need to bring friends.","done":"Ravenholdt thanks you, hero! Take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52.1,"y":39.1,"n":"Dirk Thunderwood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"97583":{"id":97583,"t":"Wriggle","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Purchase Nutritious Slime Sludge and return to your befriended excitable slime. If it seems tired, try dancing with it again to catch its attention.\nNutritious Slime Sludge","desc":"<The little slime seems delighted and is attempting to mirror your motions as you dance. It begins to look weary though.\nThe little slime hovers over a bit of sludge and absorbs it, looking slightly rejuvenated.\nIt seems all of this dancing has tuckered it out. Perhaps someone in the Undercity canals sells more of this nutritious sludge?>","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nExcitable Slime\nExperience: 10","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":51.6,"y":58.8,"n":"Excitable Slime","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"78143":{"id":78143,"t":"Secrets of the dreamers","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Secrets of the Dreamers","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nSecrets of the Dreamers (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"543":{"id":543,"t":"The Perenolde Tiara","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Perenolde Tiara to Remington Ridgewell in Stormwind.\nPerenolde Tiara Grel'borg the Miser","desc":"The Perenolde Tiara is an old heirloom of the Perenolde \"nobles\" - the ruling family of Alterac before that kingdom fell to ruin. It is said to have been crafted by master jewelers in Ironforge, and fitted with the finest of emeralds.\nWhen Alterac was destroyed the Tiara was lost, but there are rumors that an Ogre Mage, Grel'borg the Miser, found the tiara and now wanders the Ruins of Alterac searching for more treasures.\nWe would have you acquire the tiara for us.","rew":"Money: 1 50 1 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Salutations, ‹name›. Do try to avoid stepping on my pant cuffs. This outfit is newly tailored.","done":"Ah, this is splendid. This will have to be cleaned of course, but you really outdid yourself, ‹name›. I will have someone prepare the tiara and place it within our collection posthaste.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Count Remington Ridgewell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"98463":{"id":98463,"t":"Talk of the town","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Visit Nixxrax Fillamug in the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay in Stranglethorn.","desc":"Look, I'm glad to have you at my bar, and that's exactly why I'm telling you this.\nThe real party? That's over at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay. Yes, in Stranglethorn Vale--that Booty Bay.\nDon't give me that look. I know it's run by goblins. Bartenders talk, and bar patrons talk a LOT. All I'm saying is that if you want to see things get real wild, head over there.\nNixxrax Fillamug will keep you topped up, don't even worry.\nHillsbrad Foothills Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.4,"y":58.6,"n":"Barkeep Kelly","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27,"y":77.2,"n":"Nixxrax Fillamug","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"623":{"id":623,"t":"Akiris by the Bundle","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Bundle of Akiris Reeds to Privateer Groy in Theramore.\nBundle of Akiris Reeds\nProvided: Bundle of Akiris Reeds","desc":"‹name›, since I have you here, I got a message from Groy while you were gone. He mentioned bein' satisfied with the last shipment that arrived and has a client that wants some more of the stuff right away.\nI won't be headin' to Theramore for a week, but if you're willin' to make the journey, there's no reason you can't take the stuff for me.\nFeeling adventurous? You do know where Dustwallow Marsh is, doncha? I'd be careful though, Theramore can be dangerous if you're the wrong kind of crowd.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Yeah?","done":"What?! I got a lot better things to do then talk to the likes of you, ‹class›. Make it worth my while or get outta my face.\nHuh? Bloads sent ya, huh? Well, whaddaya got for me?\n<Privateer Groy looks over the bundle carefully.>\nNot bad, not bad at all. Another bundle will make my client quite happy.\nI suppose yer next question's gonna be about money, huh, ‹class›? Of course it is!\nHere, take this coin and some advice: get off my docks.\nStranglethorn Vale Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.8,"y":76.4,"n":"Privateer Bloads","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.8,"y":53.2,"n":"Privateer Groy","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8063":{"id":8063,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Bracers","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Armsplint. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Armsplint\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The madcaps of Zandalar are similar to rogues, but above all else they embrace madness... chaos... the unpredictability of existence. A terror to behold on the battlefield, they sowed the seeds of confusion and mayhem amongst our enemies in the savage times after the tribes splintered. We would not be here today without them.\nBring to me the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub that I seek, and I will grant you the first of the madcap's prized armors. Embrace the madness!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Madcap's Bracers\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Seek the madness from within Zul'Gurub and overshadow it with your own, ‹name›! To do so means success, and success means reward! Let not the Blood God reign supreme again!","done":"Well done, ‹name›... your accomplishments in Zul'Gurub have earned you the right to call the Zandalar tribe as a friend. I will see to the disposition of the Paragons; for your effort please accept this reward!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5263":{"id":5263,"t":"Above and Beyond","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to Stratholme and destroy Baron Rivendare. Take his head and return to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff.\nHead of Baron Rivendare Baron Rivendare in Stratholme","desc":"You display a natural aptitude for destruction and you follow orders. It is rare to see the two coexist. I am beginning to think that you may make an excellent vehicle of divine justice.\n<Zverenhoff clasps his hands together in front of his face.>\nKel'Thuzad's errand boy rules over Stratholme. Prove to me that you are a champion - my champion. Destroy Baron Rivendare and return to me with his head.","rew":"Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The Baron has slain more people than you have most likely seen in your lifetime.","done":"It has been many years since I have ushered a champion into our ranks. You are the first to be granted audience with Lord Maxwell in years.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"93663":{"id":93663,"t":"Lost in transit","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the missing courier, and ensure Dar's shipment is delivered to the Harborage.\nCourier's Shipment","desc":"The draenei of the Harborage are skilled fishermen, and willing to trawl more dangerous waters than I. We occasionally trade. They give us some of their catch, and I offer some of our extra supplies.\nI'd sent a goblin courier to deliver my latest shipment, but he never returned. A crocolisk likely made a meal of him.\nMore importantly, my business reputation is at stake. That shipment must be found, and delivered to the harborage. Please, find it if you can. Check near the waters along the road.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 93663","cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"1423":{"id":1423,"t":"The Lost Supplies","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Lost Supplies to Quartermaster Lungertz.\nLost Supplies Scattered Crate\nProvided: Lost Supplies","desc":"This barrel is small yet sturdy. Its seams are sealed with a yellow, pungent wax. Stamped on the bottom of the barrel are the words:\nQUARTERMASTER LUNGERTZ\nNETHERGARDE KEEP","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Supplies\nExperience: 25\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Ah, thank you ‹name›! So many supplies are lost from Darkshire to here. It's good to see that some are recovered.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":4.9,"y":31.2,"n":"Lost Supplies","s":1},{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.5,"y":21.4,"n":"Quartermaster Lungertz","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"2623":{"id":2623,"t":"The Swamp Talker","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Warchief's Orders and return them to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.\nWarchief's Orders Swamp Talker","desc":"Orders were given by the dispatch commander. We took... took orders. On way to Blasted Lands, ambushed.\nMurlocs... Many murlocs... One named Swamp Talker. Took orders from my hands as spear thrust into my skull. East... cave....\n<Bengor passes out.>","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"Awaiting orders.","done":"It is worse than I imagined. Nineteen of my men could have been spared from the agony which they faced. If only I had not acted so irrationally.\nYou must help them, ‹name›! I am powerless to act.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":45,"y":57.4,"n":"Bengor","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"863":{"id":863,"t":"The Escape","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Wizzlecrank and the stolen goblin shredder on the way to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.","desc":"I suppose I'll learn as we go... Couldn't be too hard. Just some buttons here, and a lever or two... Well, are you ready to go?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlaring Baton Greasy Tinker's Pants\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,700\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Can I help you?","done":"Hopefully we'll be able to get something of value from the wrecked shredder prototype... my time's running out! I'll dispatch a salvage team to Wizzlecrank's location on the double.\nOh, let me give you something for your trouble, too.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":56.5,"y":7.5,"n":"Wizzlecrank's Shredder","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"6543":{"id":6543,"t":"The Warsong Reports","lv":19,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Open the Bundle of Reports. Take the Warsong Reports to the Warsong Scout, Warsong Runner, and Warsong Outrider. Bring back the updates they give you to Kadrak at the northern watch tower in the barrens.\nWarsong Scout Update\nWarsong Runner Update\nWarsong Outrider Update\nProvided: Bundle of Reports","desc":"I recently deployed a few scouts into Ashenvale and I need a runner to take them their orders, and bring me back a report of what they have observed.\nYour first stop should be the Zoram'gar Outpost, along the coast to the west, at the Zoram Strand, to locate the first runner. You also need to stop at Splintertree Post, to the north, and along the road to the east, near Azshara. You will find a scout and an outrider there.\nGive them each a report, and from them, get an update on their findings.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,800\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Hurry, ‹name›. They must receive their reports; it is urgent.","done":"I can see that you are one that can be counted on. These updates are crucial to our plans to further our presence in Ashenvale. We can now plan our next move.\nThe Barrens Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.1,"y":5.4,"n":"Kadrak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96383":{"id":96383,"t":"Legacy reward spectral bear cub","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","rew":"You will receive:\nSpectral Bear Cub\nLevel 0 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 96383","cats":["the-barrens"]},"1183":{"id":1183,"t":"Goblin Sponsorship","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Fuel Regulator Blueprints to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.\nFuel Regulator Blueprints Cozzle's Footlocker\nProvided: Fuel Regulator Blueprints","desc":"You should be all set to go. Give Pozzik my regards and tell him that if he ever needs anything, not to hesitate to ask. I'll be waiting for the news that he breaks the track record soon!","rew":"Experience: 700","back":"‹name›! Did you manage to track down the fuel regulator?","done":"I was hoping that it would be already assembled, but this does present the unique opportunity to improve on the design from the ground up. Thanks, ‹name›. I'll be able to sketch up some improved schematics, build the thing, and have it installed real soon.\nStranglethorn Vale Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7663":{"id":7663,"t":"New Kodo - Green","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Green Kodo","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGreat Brown Kodo Great Gray Kodo Great White Kodo","back":"If you bring me your aging kodo, I will trade it in for one from the new herd. The new kodo will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the great kodos we already have around the yard here to see what you will have to choose from.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":62.1,"n":"Harb Clawhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"7823":{"id":7823,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":42.7,"n":"Rumstag Proudstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"383":{"id":383,"t":"Vital Intelligence","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Scarlet Crusade Documents to Executor Zygand in Brill.\nScarlet Crusade Documents Meven Korgal\nProvided: Scarlet Crusade Documents","desc":"These will need to be taken to my superior, Executor Zygand, in Brill. With this information, we'll be able to deal a decisive blow to the Scarlet Crusade. Your services have been useful here in Deathknell, but I need someone to deliver this to Zygand, and I believe he'll be able to find you more appropriate work.\nTake the road north out of Deathknell. Soon after entering Tirisfal proper, you'll hit a crossroads. Take the eastern fork, and keep going east. You'll pass Cold Hearth Manor along the way.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 0 silver, 75 copper Experience: 340\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes, what do you want?","done":"Yes, this is very good. You've done well in obtaining this information, ‹name›. Hmm... names of the officers in the Tirisfal Glades...\nImagine the blow we could deal to the morale of those bloody zealots if we were to kill their leaders in one swift strike.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.2,"y":66,"n":"Executor Arren","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4143":{"id":4143,"t":"Haze of Evil","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 5 samples of Atal'ai Haze, then return to Muigin in Un'Goro Crater.\n5 Atal'ai Haze Deep Lurker 80 % , Saturated Ooze 40 % , Murk Worm 40 %","desc":"To tell you the truth, ‹name›, I've never seen any plants like this in my travels. Perhaps I should take a trip to this crater...\nAt any rate, I think I know just the thing Muigin's looking for -- Atal'ai haze. It's horrid stuff, hard to collect, but it's just what he needs to control the little monsters.\nYou'll need to visit the temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of Sorrows. The Atal'ai Haze can be collected from the deep lurkers, murk worms, or oozes found there. Good luck, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100","back":"Larion's still not speaking to me! He sure knows how to hold a grudge.","done":"I admit, I'm a bit hesitant to touch that stuff, ‹name›! But if Gregan says it'll work, then I'm willing to give it a try!\nFeralas Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":45.1,"y":25.6,"n":"Gregan Brewspewer","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":42.9,"y":9.6,"n":"Muigin","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4383":{"id":4383,"t":"Crystal Ward","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Red Power Crystal Red Power Crystal , Red Power Crystal , Mor'vek 46.2 % , Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n10 Green Power Crystal Green Power Crystal , Green Power Crystal , Mor'vek 30.8 % , Spiked Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Ward","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine green power crystals with red power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to strengthen the protection you have against physical damage.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":23.9,"y":59.2,"n":"Western Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4783":{"id":4783,"t":"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe","lv":37,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Vials of Hatefury Blood and 1 Lesser Infernal Stone to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\n10 Vial of Hatefury Blood Hatefury Hellcaller 40 % , Hatefury Shadowstalker 40 % , Hatefury Betrayer 40 % , Hatefury Felsworn 40 % and 3 more\nLesser Infernal Stone Lesser Infernal 50 % , Demon Portal Guardian 50 %","desc":"The next components are found in Desolace, far to the west of the Barrens and even the Stonetalon Mountains.\nThere, chaos still reigns after the Sundering. Both your strength and cunning will be tested there--you will face creatures of hatred and also of the Burning Legion.\nFrom the Hatefury satyr in the northeast, bring me their blood. From the lesser infernals in Mannoroc Coven, bring me a lesser infernal stone.\nWe will use both in the construction of your robe.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Desolace is not a kind area: naga, giants, satyr, the Burning Legion... all of those and warring centaur clans all make the land dangerous if you're not careful.\nLike I said before, it will not only test your strength and cunning, but also your patience. Be wary in those lands, ‹name›.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. These will do nicely. I will prepare them now while you move on to your last two components. Are you ready?\nThe Barrens Desolace","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7583":{"id":7583,"t":"Suppression","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture forth into the Tainted Scar and locate a Doomguard Commander.\nUse the Glowing Crystal Prison on the Doomguard Commander. Be prepared for a ferocious onslaught of attacks, as the demon attempts to escape capture.\nShould you succeed, return the Imprisoned Doomguard to Daio in the Tainted Scar.\nImprisoned Doomguard Imprisoned Doomguard\nGlowing Crystal Prison\nProvided: Glowing Crystal Prison","desc":"The prison is ready. Now for the most difficult portion of this task.\nYou must find and capture a Doomguard Commander within the Tainted Scar using this crystal prison.\nBe warned! A Doomguard is a cunning and lethal adversary and will seek to destroy you as you begin the ritual of imprisonment. It will flail wildly in its attempts to escape imprisonment.\nIt will focus on nothing but you, ‹name›. Because of this, I must recommend that you take companions capable of keeping you alive!","rew":"You will receive:\nTome of Sacrifice\nYou will learn: Ritual of Doom\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Hrm? Well?","done":"You have done as I have asked. You are ready to be given the knowledge to conjure and control the beast.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":34.1,"y":50.1,"n":"Daio the Decrepit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"2383":{"id":2383,"t":"Simple Parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Parchment and speak to Frang in the Valley of Trials.\nSimple Parchment\nProvided: Simple Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the warrior trainer Frang. He would have words with you when you're ready. You'll find him outside the Den, taking cover in the shade.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What's that you have there? A parchment? You're not a scholar, I hope...","done":"Ah, that's my parchment. I heard you'd be coming to the Valley, ‹name›. I'm glad to see you made it--let's hope you survive the trials ahead. Like I said, as you gain in power, come to me--I will do what I can to train you in the ways of the warrior.\nGood luck, ‹name›, and return to me whenever you feel ready.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.9,"y":69.4,"n":"Frang","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1503":{"id":1503,"t":"Forged Steel","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Forged Steel Bars to Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.\nForged Steel Bars Stolen Iron Chest","desc":"I will give you a weapon, ‹name›, but first you must aid me. The Razormanes to the northwest came into my camp a few nights past. They would not meet me in combat, but they know my eyes are bad--a few distracted me with snorts while others stole from me! The cowards!\nThey took an iron chest, and within it were some forged steel bars. If you can recover them then I will give you the weapon you seek.\nSearch for the iron box within the quilboar camps, and return with the forged steel bars.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThun'grim's Axe Thun'grim's Mace Thun'grim's Dagger Thun'grim's Sword\nExperience: 850","back":"Do you have my steel bars?","done":"You found them! And all the bars are here, which doesn't surprise me. I didn't think the Razormanes would know what to do with fine steel like this.\nThank you, ‹name›. Here is your reward. May it serve you well.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1823":{"id":1823,"t":"Speak with Ruga","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ruga Ragetotem.","desc":"You are a warrior of skill and growing renown. Perhaps you are ready for Ruga Ragetotem's trial? If so, then find Ruga in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nHe awaits those warriors who answer his call.","rew":"Experience: 160","done":"You are here for my trial, ‹name›?\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Sorek","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.7,"y":59.4,"n":"Ruga Ragetotem","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5023":{"id":5023,"t":"Better Late Than Never","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check with the Royal Overseers of the Undercity to learn the whereabouts of a Jeremiah Felstone. There is usually a census officer located near guild and tabard registration.\nJanice's Parcel\nProvided: Janice's Parcel","desc":"You pick up the package, wiping off a small layer of dust and grime that had settled on it. It is addressed in a hurried hand to a Jeremiah Felstone of Lordaeron; the delivery of the package is dated for well over four years ago.\nThough it is unclear if Jeremiah Felstone is even alive, it is widely known that the Undercity, formerly known as Lordaeron, keeps records on the populace of the city. This is handled through the Royal Overseers of the Undercity Census.","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"Are you here to seek the assistance of the Undercity census, or just to ask me if someone you knew is dead? I get asked that a lot.","done":"A package for a Jeremiah Felstone, with his last known address as Lordaeron... I should be able to assist you.\nJeremiah Felstone was in the city before the plague. Well, I should say the former Jeremiah Felstone - some of the Forsaken have changed their last names to rid themselves of their former countenance. This case is no exception; the former Jeremiah Felstone is now known as Jeremiah Payson.\nWait a minute... isn't he the cockroach vendor?\nWestern Plaguelands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.7,"y":55.2,"n":"Janice's Parcel","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":69.8,"y":43.2,"n":"Royal Overseer Bauhaus","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5903":{"id":5903,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands.\nEmpty Termite Jar\n100 Plagueland Termites Large Termite Mound\nProvided: Empty Termite Jar","desc":"I've tried many times to rout out the Scarlet Crusade through force alone, but to no avail. So, as an alternative, I've decided to make their lives more difficult.\nIf you are willing to help, I want to infest that lumber mill with the most terrible species of termites ever found.\nIn Plaguewood, near the once-great Stratholme, there is a breed that survived the plague and the Scourge combined. Find their mounds and fill this jar with them, so we can prepare them to be unleashed on the Crusade.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Did you find the termite mounds, ‹name›? I've heard they are all over Plaguewood.","done":"These will do nicely, ‹name›. Thank you.\nIf you're ready, we can get on with the next step.\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.4,"y":84.8,"n":"Nathaniel Dumah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"463":{"id":463,"t":"The Greenwarden","lv":21,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Greenwarden.","desc":"You've heard of the Greenwarden? You're not looking for him, are you? Well I say you're crazy if you are, but who am I to keep a fool from his/her death?\nIf you are seeking that beast, then I hear he is in the marsh, east of the road where it forks to Dun Modr. He's lurking there among the crocs...and worse!\nAnd leave your money here. You won't need it where you're going...and you don't want to chip ol' Greenie's tooth on your gold when he bites you in half, do you?","rew":"Experience: 825","done":"The roots and ferns speak well of you, small one. Although I have many names, I answer to only a few. But you may call me Rethiel.\nAnd you must harken...for these lands weep from festered wounds, and I would charge you to heal them.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.9,"y":59.6,"n":"First Mate Fitzsimmons","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"303":{"id":303,"t":"The Dark Iron War","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Motley Garmason at Dun Modr wants you to kill 10 Dark Iron Dwarves, 5 Dark Iron Tunnelers, 5 Dark Iron Saboteurs and 5 Dark Iron Demolitionists.\nDark Iron Dwarf slain : 0/ 10\nDark Iron Tunneler slain : 0/ 5\nDark Iron Saboteur slain : 0/ 5\nDark Iron Demolitionist slain : 0/ 5","desc":"War rages both home and abroad. While mighty Dwarven soldiers give their lives in far off territories in the name of the Alliance, our own lands fall prey to the evil deeds of the Dark Iron Dwarves. They laid waste to the Thandol Span. Dun Modr fell soon after.\nWe need you to gather force and push the front back. If you can kill 10 Dark Iron Dwarves, 5 Tunnelers, 5 Saboteurs and 5 Demolitionists, the reserve might arrive in time to finish the drive.\nNow make haste!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Roggo has been unable to contact the reserve forces. We need offensive pressure on that Dark Iron encampment, ‹class›. Now get back out there and serve your duty to King Magni!","done":"You upheld your orders well, ‹class›. You have proven yourself to be a valiant soldier and loyal servant to King Magni and for that I salute you! With the pressure you applied to the Dark Iron encampment, we now stand a chance of driving them off our lands for good. . .if only the damned reserve would show. . . .","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.7,"y":18.2,"n":"Motley Garmason","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98223":{"id":98223,"t":"Old habits","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Tattered Spellbook to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor.\nProvided: Tattered Spellbook","desc":"This book has been badly burned--perhaps by the dragonfire that destroyed much of the Dragonmaw clan.\nOf what little is legible, it seems to describe rituals relating to the use of the Demon Soul that the clan had used to control the dragons.\nIt is far too incomplete to be of real use, but based on roughly inserted pages on animal hide it seems Nek'rosh had attempted to salvage it. Freshly dried ink mentions a \"Shadow Council.\"\nCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor would want to know about this.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlamescarred Spellbook Dragonmaw Buckler\nExperience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":53.5,"y":54.5,"n":"Tattered Spellbook","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4863":{"id":4863,"t":"Enraged Wildkin","lv":59,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked wagon.","desc":"Looking around, you don't see much that Jaron could want here. However, you do notice that the crate you found has been smashed open, almost as if this was what the wildkin were after...\nLooking to the east, you can barely make out an abandoned wagon. Perhaps you might find Jaron's things there. It's worth a look.","rew":"Experience: 3,200","done":"Approaching the wagon, it doesn't appear that there is much more here for Jaron. But, looking on the ground, you notice some crates that look undamaged, despite being half-buried in the snow.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":59,"y":59.8,"n":"Damaged Crate","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.4,"y":60.7,"n":"Jaron's Wagon","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92463":{"id":92463,"t":"The cirrusfly queen","lv":3,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Destroy the Cirrusfly Queen in Thendal Grove.\nCirrusfly Queen slain","desc":"If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.\nGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.\nPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nExterminator's Vest Gardening Pants Watcher's Mail Chest\nMoney: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 320\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"Cirrusflies aren't to be underestimated. They might not seem dangerous, but you have to watch out for the bigger ones. The bigger they are, the meaner!","done":"Excellent work, Dogwalker. You'd make a fine ranger if this whole \"adventurer\" thing doesn't work out for you.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.4,"y":24.8,"n":"Elatrell Featherlight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92703":{"id":92703,"t":"Deliver the news","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Alvarion Windfield in Valanaar.","desc":"I guess it doesn't feel quite right to keep calling you stranger after all of this so... thank you, ‹name›.\nIf you wouldn't mind and are back out that way, please let Alvarion know what happened here. Also, tell him that once he's up on his feet he needs to bring a windshaper back here to look at that construct for us to make sure it's safe to have around our... our family.\n<Aamelia touches her belly gently.>\nHe doesn't know about this part. Let's just keep that bit between us for now.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPlanting Shovel Roofing Hammer Trusty Wrench\nExperience: 600\n+100 reputation with Windshapers\n+100 reputation with High Order","done":"<Alvarion's eyes tear up as you finish retelling the story of what happened at the orchard.>\nI don't know how to thank you, friend. I came to Valanaar looking for hope. A vain hope, I was almost certain. But instead I found a hero. A real hero, like the stories from before we came to Skywall.\nI'll never forget what you did for us, Orsen. You'll always be welcome at the Windfield home.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":62,"y":73.2,"n":"Alvarion Windfield","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8143":{"id":8143,"t":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zandalarian Shadow Talisman","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalarian Shadow Talisman\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I sense that you have dealt countless fatalities to the Hakkari, ‹name›. You carry the stink of their mojo.\nI assume the Shadow talisman has assisted in the culling? Give it to me and allow me to enhance its power.","done":"An assassin of your caliber should be given a wide berth. Your foes must learn respect! You will get just that when the enemy sees the glint of Death's Hand - all too late...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});